.TH START_VNC_TUNNELS_MU2E.SH 1 "2026-10-06" "mu2edaq-controlroom t01.00.00" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
start_vnc_tunnels_mu2e.sh \- open or close a range of ssh port forwards to a gateway for VNC (deprecated)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bin/start_vnc_tunnels_mu2e.sh
.RB [ \-h
.IR host ]
.RB [ \-u
.IR user ]
.RB [ \-p
.IR start_port ]
.RB [ \-n
.IR num_ports ]
.RB [ \-k ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Deprecated.
Superseded by
.BR crs\-tunnel (1)
and
.BR crs\-gui (1)
from
.BR mu2edaq\-controlroom\-setup ,
whose tunnel code states that it generalizes this script
.RB ( tunnels.py:5 ).
.PP
A
.B zsh
script.
It checks for a ticket with
.BR "klist \-\-test" ,
then for every port
.I P
from
.I start_port
to
.IR start_port + num_ports ,
.B inclusive
(six tunnels with the defaults), runs
.PP
.EX
ssh \-f \-N \-M \-S /tmp/ssh\-ctrl\-HOST\-P \-L P:localhost:P \-l USER HOST
.EE
.PP
The far end of each forward is the gateway's own loopback, so this
assumes VNC servers or static tunnels listening on the gateway at
5951\(en5956; the current control room instead forwards through the
gateway to
.I localhost:590N
on each session host.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-h " host"
gateway (default
.BR mu2edaq\-gateway.fnal.gov ,
not the
.B mu2egateway01.fnal.gov
the current tools use).
.TP
.BI \-u " user"
login (default
.BR mu2eshift ).
.TP
.BI \-p " start_port"
first port (default 5951).
.TP
.BI \-n " num_ports"
default 5; one more tunnel than this is opened.
.TP
.B \-k
close the range with
.BR "ssh \-O exit" ,
then exit 1.
.SH FILES
.I /tmp/ssh\-ctrl\-HOST\-PORT
control sockets, in a world\-writable directory.
.SH EXIT STATUS
1 with no ticket, and always after
.BR \-k ;
otherwise the status of the last
.B ssh
or
.BR echo .
.B klist \-\-test
is Heimdal syntax: MIT
.B klist
(Linux) rejects it, so on Linux the script always reports
"No Kerberos Ticket found" and exits 1.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
zsh bin/start_vnc_tunnels_mu2e.sh \-h mu2egateway01.fnal.gov \-u mu2edaq \-p 5951 \-n 2
zsh bin/start_vnc_tunnels_mu2e.sh \-k
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR crs\-tunnel (1),
.BR crs\-gui (1),
.BR ssh (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Andrew Norman, Mu2e DAQ group, Fermilab.
